AI-Powered Academic Article Analysis & Turkish NLP Platform

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, Python NLP engineer, UI/UX designer, and application security specialist. Build a professional, modern, fully functional web application called LexiMind.

This is a university Natural Language Processing (NLP) project. It must be a real working application, not just a visual prototype. The application must demonstrate genuine NLP processing with Python, Gensim Word2Vec, a backend API, document processing, and a polished frontend.

Do not build a generic chatbot. The primary purpose is to analyze academic articles and automatically extract meaningful keywords and phrases.

All user-facing interface text must be in Turkish. Use English for code identifiers, filenames, and technical documentation where appropriate.

1. PROJECT OBJECTIVES

Build LexiMind with these core capabilities:

Upload academic articles in PDF, DOCX, and TXT formats.

Paste article text directly into the application.

Extract and rank important keywords and multi-word phrases.

Display keyword relevance, frequency, and supporting context where available.

Use Gensim Word2Vec for semantic similarity and related-word discovery.

Provide a clean analysis history for registered users.

Allow results to be exported to CSV or TXT.

Include functional user authentication and profile settings.

Include Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, and Cookie Policy pages.

Provide a responsive, accessible, polished dashboard suitable for a university project demonstration.

The interface must look like a credible academic software product rather than a template or a simple student demo.

